nventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UOSAKI YUKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMANO, MASAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARA, MITSUNOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEDA, SHUN-ICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANAZAWA, JUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANDA, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIIKE, YOKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UOSAKI, YUKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Apoptosis inducing agents which contain as the active ingredient tetrocarcin derivatives represented by general formula (I) or salts thereof. These agents are useful as drugs for preventing and/or treating diseases caused by the accelerated expression of proteins of the Bc1-2 family such as cancer and AIDS; wherein &lt;u&gt;---&lt;/u&gt; represents a single or double bond; j and k are each 0 or 1; R&lt;1&gt; to R&lt;3&gt;, R&lt;7&gt; to R&lt;10&gt; and R&lt;14&gt; represent each hydrogen, lower alkyl, etc.; R&lt;4&gt;, R&lt;11&gt;, R&lt;12&gt;, R&lt;13&gt; and R&lt;15&gt; to R&lt;18&gt; represent each hydrogen, hydroxy, lower alkyl, etc.; R&lt;5&gt; and R&lt;6&gt; represent each hydrogen, hydroxy, lower alkyl or (B) (wherein R&lt;32&gt; represents formyl, etc.; and R&lt;33&gt; to R&lt;35&gt; represent each hydrogen, hydroxy, lower alkyl, etc.); and R&lt;19&gt; represents hydroxy, lower alkoxy, lower alkanoyloxy, etc.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne des agents induisant l'apoptose qui contiennent en qualité d'ingrédient actif des dérivés de tetrocarcine correspondant à la formule générale (I) où: &lt;u&gt;---&lt;/u&gt; représente une liaison simple ou double; j et k représentent chacun 0 ou 1; R&lt;1&gt; à R&lt;3&gt;, R&lt;7&gt; à R&lt;10&gt; et R&lt;14&gt; représentent chacun hydrogène, alkyle inférieur, etc.; R&lt;4&gt;, R&lt;11&gt;, R&lt;12&gt;, R&lt;13&gt; et R&lt;15&gt; à R&lt;18&gt; représentent chacun hydrogène, hydroxy, alkyle inférieur, etc.; R&lt;5&gt; et R&lt;6&gt; représentent chacun hydrogène, hydroxy, alkyle inférieur ou (B) dans laquelle R&lt;32&gt; représente formyle etc., tandis que R&lt;33&gt; à R&lt;35&gt; représentent chacun hydrogène, hydroxy, alkyle inférieur, etc.; et R&lt;19&gt; représente hydroxy, alcoxy inférieur, alcanoyloxy inférieur, etc. Cette invention concerne également des sels de ces agents. Ces agents peuvent être utilisés en qualité de médicaments afin de prévenir et/ou de traiter des maladies dues à l'expression accélérée de protéines de la famille Bc1-2, tel que le cancer ou le SIDA.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>